{
  "turn_number": 3,
  "player_text": "I keep my voice down. A number, then. What are you charging for one bowl right now, and who are these right people?",
  "visible_motivation": "He hedged that prices shift with rumors and the guards, and that sure warmth means paying more or knowing the right people. I want a current price and who he means.",
  "intended_meaning": "Get the current stew price and who can actually provide a dry meal.",
  "generated_candidate": "\"Honestly, I can't give you a solid number right now,\" the tavern runner says, lowering their voice further as rain splatters around you. \"Prices shift with the rumors and the guards' moods. As for who the right people are—well, those vary just as much. If you want sure warmth or solid information, you might need to pay a bit more or have the right acquaintance. It's not the sort of thing I can just name out loud in this crowd.\"",
